0::/user.slice/user-1000.slice/user@1000.service/app.slice/run-r3fdc35fc80bb40bdbbab7fa75b25a9c9.scope
268435456
0
```

Observed exit: 0 (tool completed without error).

A second already-completed composition probe proved CPU lock holder and scope command run together. Exact command:
```sh
set -e; flock -x /tmp/cir-fix-all-20261120-cpu.lock systemd-run --user --scope -p MemoryMax=256M -p MemorySwapMax=0 /usr/bin/env sh -c 'p=$(awk -F: '\''$1==0 {print $3}'\'' /proc/self/cgroup); printf "pid=%s cgroup=%s memory.max=" $$ "$p"; cat /sys/fs/cgroup${p}/memory.max; sleep 0.15'
```

