Derived safe command prefix for later campaign use (not run for GPU job):
```sh
flock -x /tmp/cir-fix-all-20261120-cpu.lock systemd-run --user --scope -p MemoryMax=12G -p MemorySwapMax=0 --setenv=OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 --setenv=OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 --setenv=MKL_NUM_THREADS=1 --setenv=NUMEXPR_NUM_THREADS=1 <command>
```
GPU jobs must place the whole process tree under equivalent scope while holding `/tmp/cir_gpu.lock`; do not start one before fresh job/GPU census and owner clearance. Scope probe only verifies transient user cgroup property behavior, not GPU application or model runtime.